Part A: R = 20000 samples of size n = 50
  Poisson mean    : Var(xbar) = 0.03966, CRLB lam/n = 0.04000
  Exponential rate: Var(1/xbar) = 0.005398, CRLB rate^2/n = 0.005000
                    bias = 0.0103 (theory rate/(n-1) = 0.0102)

Part B: Cauchy location, n = 20, R = 4000
  Var(MLE) = 0.1150; 1/I(theta) = 2/n = 0.1000
  observed information: min 0.87, median 10.66, max 23.97 (expected 10.0)
  coverage of 95% Wald intervals:
    expected information: 0.928
    observed information: 0.938
  Var(MLE | J below median) = 0.1486, mean 1/J = 0.1365
  Var(MLE | J above median) = 0.0811, mean 1/J = 0.0756
